# Coding standards

- Python 3.11+; type hints on public functions; Pydantic models at boundaries.
- Prefer small pure functions; side effects in services/brokers.
- Use `structlog` via `get_logger`; include `guidance=` on operational warnings.
- Raise `TradingBotError` subclasses with actionable `guidance` for UI.
- Ruff + mypy clean for changed files; pytest for new branches.
- No bare `except:`; catch specific errors or `Exception` with logging.
- Keep modules layered — strategies must not import FastAPI; brokers must not import UI.
